# Data files are regenerated wholesale by the pipeline, so a re-run produces a
# 100k+ line diff that no reviewer reads. `-diff` keeps them fully tracked and
# versioned (nothing is lost, `git show` still has every byte) but renders the
# change as "Binary files differ" so code review stays readable.
*.csv -diff
*.jsonl -diff

# Not deliberately set: `* text=auto`. It would fix the LF/CRLF warnings but
# renormalizes every tracked file at once, which is exactly the giant unreadable
# diff this file exists to prevent. Do it alone, in its own commit.
